      "dom_id": "question-81622",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $(X∨Y)∧(X∨¬Z)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we can factor out the disjunction with $X,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(X∨Y)∧(X∨¬Z)≡X∨(Y∧¬Z)\n$$\n\nNow, since $Y∧¬Z≡¬Z∧Y,$ we can write\n\n$$\nX∨(Y∧¬Z)≡X∨(¬Z∧Y).\n$$",
